a. Write a program to work with props and states.
 props
 Definition: Props are used to pass data from one component to another (like function 
arguments in JavaScript).
 Nature: Read-only (cannot be changed by the component that receives them).
 Use: Reusable components, you can send different values each time.
States
 Definition: State is data that is managed inside a component.
 Nature: Mutable (can be updated).
 Use: To make web pages interactive (like counters, messages, etc.).
